      },
      "text": "```\n  PITTING CORROSION (Pinhole Leaks):\n    Soft water / low pH water attacks copper oxide passive layer\n    Most common: Pacific Northwest, Arizona\n    CO₂ dissolved in groundwater → carbonic acid → pH drops\n    Prevention: pH adjustment, zinc orthophosphate dosing\n    Recognition: small blue-green stains on copper pipe exterior;\n                pinhole with green/blue mineral deposit around it\n    Solution: switch to PEX, install pH neutralizer, or\n              raise hot water heater temperature (bacteria control\n              may conflict with scald prevention — balance required)"
    },
